PRD — Simple Recruitment Portal for Telesales
1. Product Overview
Build a simple, mobile-first recruitment portal for hiring Telesales Representatives.
The system should allow candidates to:
View the telesales job opportunity.
Understand responsibilities, salary, commission structure, requirements, and employment terms.
Submit an application.
Receive confirmation and stage updates through email and WhatsApp.
Receive interview scheduling information when shortlisted.
The internal recruitment team should have a simple admin dashboard where they can:
View all applicants.
Review applications.
Filter applicants.
Move applicants through recruitment stages.
Schedule interviews.
Track interview attendance.
Mark candidates as recruited or rejected.
Send automatic email and WhatsApp notifications when an applicant's stage changes.
This is intended to be a lightweight recruitment application, not a full HR management system.

2. Primary Goal
Create a fast and simple system that allows the company to recruit a large number of telesales representatives without managing applicants manually through spreadsheets, WhatsApp chats, and email.
The system should provide one clear recruitment pipeline:
Application → Review → Interview → Recruited
The experience should be simple enough for applicants to complete entirely from a mobile phone.

3. User Types
Candidate
A person applying for the Telesales role.
Candidates do not require a traditional account/password.
Their application can be identified using:
Application ID
Email address
Phone number
Admin / Recruitment Team
Internal users responsible for reviewing and managing applicants.
Admins must log in before accessing recruitment information.

4. Public Recruitment Page
Create a clean, modern, mobile-first recruitment landing page.
Suggested URL:
/careers/telesales
The page should contain the following sections.
Job Title
Telesales Representative
Job Summary
A short explanation of the role and what the candidate will be responsible for.
Example:
The Telesales Representative will contact potential customers, introduce the company's products/services, explain their benefits, follow up with prospects, and convert qualified prospects into paying customers.
Responsibilities
Example responsibilities:
Make outbound calls to prospective customers.
Introduce and explain the company's products or services.
Understand customer needs and recommend appropriate solutions.
Follow up with interested prospects.
Convert qualified prospects into paying customers.
Maintain accurate records of calls and customer conversations.
Update sales activities and customer information.
Meet daily, weekly, and monthly sales targets.
Attend required sales training and team meetings.
Maintain professional communication with prospects and customers.
Requirements
Example:
Good spoken English.
Strong communication skills.
Comfortable speaking with customers on the phone.
Ability to follow up consistently.
Basic smartphone and internet literacy.
Ability to work toward sales targets.
Previous telesales or customer service experience is an advantage but may not be mandatory.
Compensation
Compensation information should be configurable from the admin/backend.
Display:
Salary Range
₦[Minimum Salary] – ₦[Maximum Salary] per month
Commission
Clearly explain the sales commission structure.
For example:
Commission per successful sale.
Performance bonuses where applicable.
Monthly or weekly commission payment terms.
The exact salary and commission numbers must be editable without changing application code.
Employment Terms
Display information such as:
Full-time / Part-time
Remote / Hybrid / On-site
Working days
Working hours
Probation period, if applicable
Performance expectations
Payment schedule
All terms should be editable from the backend.
Call to Action
Primary button:
Apply Now
This should scroll to or open the application form.

