6. Application Completion Tracking
The system should distinguish between:
Started Application
Candidate has entered enough information to identify them, such as email or phone number, but has not submitted the application.
Completed Application
Candidate successfully submitted the full application.
Where technically practical, partially completed applications should be saved so recruitment administrators can see abandonment numbers.

7. Application Confirmation
After successful submission, show a confirmation page.
Example message:
Application Submitted Successfully
Thank you for applying for the Telesales Representative position.
Our recruitment team will review your application. If you are selected for the next stage, you will receive an update through email and WhatsApp.
Application ID:
APP-XXXXXX
The candidate should also receive the same confirmation through email.
WhatsApp confirmation can also be sent where configured.

8. Recruitment Pipeline
Every completed application should have a recruitment status.
Use the following primary stages:
1. Application Received
Candidate has completed the application.
2. Under Review
Recruitment team is reviewing the candidate.
3. Interview
Candidate has been selected and scheduled for an interview.
Interview sub-status:
Not Scheduled
Scheduled
Attended
Did Not Attend
4. Recruited
Candidate successfully passed the recruitment process.
Additional Status
Include:
Rejected
This can happen from the Review or Interview stage.
Optional:
Withdrawn
Candidate is no longer interested.

