13. Applicant Stage Management
Admin should be able to change an applicant's stage directly from their profile.
Example:
Application Received → Under Review
Under Review → Interview
Interview → Recruited
or
Under Review → Rejected
Interview → Rejected
Every stage change should:
Update the applicant record.
Store the date/time of the change.
Record which admin made the change.
Trigger the appropriate notification where required.

14. Interview Scheduling
When an applicant is moved to Interview, the admin should be able to enter:
Interview Date
Interview Time
Time Zone
Interview Type
Options:
Phone Call
WhatsApp Call
Google Meet
Physical Interview
Other
If online:
Meeting Link
If physical:
Interview Address
Optional:
Interview instructions
After scheduling, the applicant receives an email and WhatsApp message.

15. Interview Attendance
After the interview date, the recruiter should be able to mark:
Attended
Did Not Attend
The dashboard should calculate attendance totals from this information.

16. Notifications
The application should support:
Email
WhatsApp
Notifications should be triggered automatically for important recruitment events.
Application Submitted
Email subject:
We Received Your Application
Inform the candidate that the application has been successfully received.
Selected for Interview
Send:
Applicant name
Interview date
Interview time
Interview format
Meeting link/address
Instructions
Example message:
"Congratulations, {{first_name}}. You have been selected for the interview stage for the Telesales Representative position.
Your interview is scheduled for {{date}} at {{time}}.
Interview method: {{interview_type}}
{{meeting_link_or_address}}
Please ensure you are available at the scheduled time."
Interview Reminder
Optional but recommended.
Send a reminder:
24 hours before interview.
Recruited
Send a congratulatory message informing the applicant that they have successfully completed the recruitment process and explaining the next step.
Rejected
Send a professional rejection message.
Example:
"Thank you for your interest in joining our team. After reviewing your application, we will not be progressing your application further at this time.
We appreciate the time you invested in the recruitment process."

17. Notification Templates
Notification text should not be hard-coded.
Admins should be able to configure templates for:
